# Experiments and statistics

- Split by **subject**, never by trial. Validation is carved from training subjects only; test subjects never
  influence model selection (guarded in `e2e_trainer.py`; keep `curves: false` during the pilot/main runs).
- Normalisation/alignment must be per-trial fit-free or use only the *same session's unlabeled trials*
  (EA whitening per session; AdaBN re-estimates BN statistics on the held-out subject's unlabeled trials,
  evaluation-time only, `adabn_*` columns, not part of the cell signature). No statistics cross subjects.
  EA/AdaBN are transductive-unsupervised: the paper says so, and ANN references run the same alignment arm.
- Recipe = benchmark recipe: Adam 1e-4, batch 128, no scheduler, max 500 epochs, patience 25 on macro-F1,
  training seed 0, split seeds 41 and 42. `cross_subject` blocks of all `snn_*.yaml` are identical to the
  18-entry benchmark so every entry pairs per (split, fold, subject) with the ANN baselines.
- Pre-registered family (2C, Holm, α=0.05, 5 tests): H0-NI (S@hplif vs eegnex, unaligned, δ=1pp, one-sided
  bootstrap lower bound); **H1 = the only primary test** (difference-of-differences Wilcoxon, S-EEGNeX-S@hplif,
  EA+AdaBN vs none, accuracy, best-val); H2-NI (S vs D, δ=1pp); H3 (Page's L: LIF ≤ PLIF ≤ HetPLIF);
  B1 (S-EEGNeX vs S-EEGNet). SHU/3C are replication cohorts; everything else is exploratory.
- Two main tables, never mixed: unaligned block (18 ANN + unaligned SNN; Friedman + Nemenyi CD, Bonferroni–Dunn
  vs S-EEGNeX, k=19) and the aligned block ({eegnex, eegnet_official, S-EEGNeX} × {none, EA, EA+AdaBN}, i.e. 3×3;
  H1 uses the {EEGNeX, S-EEGNeX} × {none, EA+AdaBN} 2×2 subset).
- `scripts/analyze_snn_round.py` writes the pre-registered family and H1 against the roles `zs` / `ea`; the main
  run's aligned arm is labelled `eaz`, so always pass `--aligned-arm eaz` (the script aborts otherwise).
- Tests: exact Wilcoxon for n ≤ 50, permutation for n = 51; Hodges–Lehmann shift + BCa bootstrap CI; report
  n_eff and win/tie/loss; assert `n_cells == n_folds × n_splits`. SHU primary metric = balanced accuracy.
- Energy: per-layer dense MACs × measured firing rate (45 nm: MAC 4.6 pJ, AC 0.9 pJ); reference = EEGNet ANN
  and S-EEGNet; multipliers never in title/abstract.
- Tables are generated by scripts from `result.json`; never hand-edit numbers. Never fabricate or extrapolate.
